Description: Linux hardening auditor (CIS benchmark mapping) — core package
 BOB (Bodyguard Of Bits) audits a Linux system against a curated set of
 hardening checks (firewall, SSH, kernel sysctl, services, file permissions,
 MAC policy, auditd, …) and reports findings with severity levels.
 .
 BOB is audit-only: it does not modify system state without explicit user
 confirmation. A --fix mode prompts before each remediation; --offline
 disables all outbound network calls for air-gapped environments.
 .
 This package ships the core audit pipeline and the headless CLI. For the
 interactive curses TUI (--install-cron / --manage-cron / --manage-logs
 wizards), install the optional bob-tui package as well.

Package: bob
Architecture: all
Depends:
 bob-core (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: Linux hardening auditor (CIS benchmark mapping) — meta-package
 Convenience meta-package pulling in both bob-core and bob-tui for a
 full BOB installation. Most users want this package.
 .
 See bob-core (the audit engine without the curses TUI) and bob-tui
 (the interactive wizards) for split installations, e.g. in minimal
 containers or build sandboxes where curses is unwanted.

Package: bob-tui
Architecture: all
Depends:
 bob-core (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${python3:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 python3-curses-pyx:any | python3:any,
Description: Linux hardening auditor (CIS benchmark mapping) — curses TUI
 Optional curses-based interactive wizards for BOB: --install-cron,
 --manage-cron, --manage-logs, the interactive --explain picker, and
 future TUI flows.
 .
 Install this on workstations where the interactive flows are wanted.
 Headless servers and CI runners typically only need bob-core.
